---
import Slide from '../ui/Slide.astro';
import Matrix from '../ui/Matrix.astro';
import Callout from '../ui/Callout.astro';
---

<Slide
  id="s53-interview"
  chapter="Interview Prep"
  title="Interview Bank — Questions 1–8"
  notes="Rapid-fire practice — systematic thinking, not trivia. Q1: Running vs Ready — probe semantics. Q2: Events first — free, structured, timestamped. Q3: Pending — always describe pod for scheduler message. Q4: OOM 137 — cgroup kill, not app exit code. Q5: Endpoints — bridge between Service and Ready pods. Q6: DNS ndots — classic FQDN vs short name bug. Q7: NetworkPolicy default-deny blocks until explicit allow. Q8: rollout undo — fastest revert, not delete pods. Pause after each — ask audience before revealing. Continues on next slide."
>
  <div class="stagger flex flex-col gap-6">
    <Matrix
      headers={['#', 'Question', 'Ideal Answer (1 line)']}
      rows={[
        ['1', 'Pod Running but not serving traffic — why?', 'Not Ready → excluded from Endpoints; check readiness probe & conditions'],
        ['2', 'First command for any broken pod?', 'kubectl describe pod — Events section before logs'],
        ['3', 'Pod Pending forever — where to look?', 'describe pod Events: FailedScheduling message (resources, affinity, taints)'],
        ['4', 'Exit code 137 meaning?', 'OOMKilled — cgroup memory limit exceeded; check limits & memory metrics'],
        ['5', 'Service exists but no traffic reaches pods?', 'kubectl get endpoints — empty subsets = no Ready backends'],
        ['6', 'Intermittent DNS failures in Java apps?', 'Check ndots / search domains — FQDN vs short name resolution'],
        ['7', 'Default-deny NetworkPolicy — what breaks first?', 'All egress/ingress blocked until explicit allow rules added'],
        ['8', 'Fastest rollback after bad deploy?', 'kubectl rollout undo deployment/X — don\'t delete pods manually'],
      ]}
    />

    <Callout type="framework">
      Questions 9–32 continue on the next slides. Think in layers, not commands.
    </Callout>
  </div>
</Slide>
